# dasmxx x86 fixes required by this baseline
#
# Apply to a clean checkout of https://github.com/nejohnson/dasmxx at commit
# 23af0f649268c17644fa1ab9ae0594e93b67721e, then `cd src && make dasmx86`:
#
#     git -C ~/iomoon/tools/dasmxx apply .../dasmxx-x86-fixes.patch
#
# Contents (see ../README.md for the full write-up):
#   * Task 3: the 80186 opcode extensions (PUSH/IMUL imm, ENTER/LEAVE,
#     shift-by-imm8, PUSHA/POPA/BOUND/INS/OUTS).
#   * Task 4: near-branch targets wrapped inside the segment; a new 'g'
#     command giving each region its CS base; the ADC entry of the 80/81/83
#     group fixed (it used mask value 0x80, outside the 0x38 REG mask, so it
#     never matched) and the 0x83 form added for AND/OR/XOR; the F6/F7
#     unary group un-mapped from FE/FF (this both hid MUL/DIV/NEG/NOT behind
#     a catch-all TEST that swallowed following bytes, and hijacked the FF
#     group's CALL/JMP/PUSH); a bounds check on MOV Sreg with REG >= 4,
#     which previously handed operand() a wild pointer and crashed;
#     cross-references and a {flat} annotation for far pointers; and the max
#     instruction length raised from 5 to 8 bytes.
#
# The patch is kept here because the dasmxx checkout lives outside this
# repository and its changes are not committed there.
